# The Record menu: opened with Alt-C on the item list, its Open choosing
# item 1; on the item form its own verbs, Used with it opening the Loans
# tab on what is used with the item, where Ctrl-L, a loan, does nothing
# and the menu offers no Lend, a service record opened from the item's
# tab offering no Open item, and Back leaving the form.  Ctrl-L on item 2
# opens a new loan of it, left unsaved.  In the loans and holds, Ctrl-R
# asks for the item to reserve (left with Esc), Ctrl-PgUp goes back from
# the open rows to every row, and Ctrl-L there lends item 2, the loan's
# form in view mode offering Edit and Back.  The menus of the location
# form, the user form and the category form hold only Back, and the user
# list's and the category list's own verbs are back once their form is
# left.
